      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "Demas Lindley built a fort in 1773 that later became a stone monument on Route 18, marking early frontier defense.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        4,
        5,
        6
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prosperity_pennsylvania",
      "category": "landmark",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Local farms like Elysian Fields produce lamb while Seldom Seen Farm offers riding lessons, showcasing Prosperity's rural charm.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        14
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prosperity_pennsylvania",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "Prosperity stretches along Route 18, about nine miles south of Washington and 37 miles southwest of Pittsburgh, near the state border.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        18,
        19
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prosperity_pennsylvania",
      "category": "other",
      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "The community sits in the Chartiers Creek watershed, feeding into the Monongahela River basin.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        20
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://grokipedia.com/page/prosperity_pennsylvania",
      "category": "nature",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "Prosperity experiences a humid continental climate with July highs around 82°F and January lows near 24°F, plus roughly 31 inches of snow each winter.",
